cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "mhs: mollified Mindlin half-space Green's functions for triangular dislocation elements"
abstract: >-
  Mollified Mindlin half-space triangular-dislocation Green's functions, as
  matrices, for a homogeneous half space with no topography. Following Cortez's
  method of regularized Stokeslets, the point force is replaced by a smooth blob
  of width epsilon and the elastostatic equations are then solved exactly for
  that body force, so the kernels are singular nowhere and still satisfy the
  equations of static elasticity. A fault therefore has a finite width, and
  stress is defined on the fault itself. The free surface is carried by Mindlin
  image terms rather than by a meshed boundary. The library builds the on-fault
  interaction matrices used in static stress transfer, rate-and-state and
  earthquake-cycle models.
